{title:Impossible Things}
{key:}

A dandelion clock landed on the river
And floated slowly towards the sea
I took this as conclusive evidence
That the fish wish to speak with me

I waited at the riverside for their arrival
On a gloriously perfect summer’s day
A salmon head rose up from the river
And this is what it had to say

It said “Never trust a dandelion clock
Floating seaward from the shore
It will make you believe that impossible things
Are not impossible any more”

Crestfallen, I ran away from the river
With all sorts of impossibilities on my mind
I went in search of any other impossible thing
But not a single one did I find

So now I’m all confused
And maybe you are too
Just steer away from those dandelion clocks
Because the fish might start talking to you
